{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516609-dark-kingdom-of-emerald","id":1516609,"title":"Dark Kingdom of... Emerald?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-28T22:33:53-07:00","id":1516609,"title":"Dark Kingdom of... Emerald?","content":"I'm planning a game in Brazil... or more or less that area, South America. Shapeshifters, Drowned Legacies, Cainites and all, I have that covered... <br /> ...but I have faint memories about that local Dark Kingdom, but to be honest my memory kind of betrayed me at this point<br /> On one hand, I remember the Dark Kingdom of Gold (guess from El Dorado, and such)<br /> Central Amercia was under the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian, while Dark Kingdom of Flint was the domain of the wraithly natives of North America. <br /> Buuuut... for some reason I have a lingering memory about the Dark Kingdom of Emerald (witch is also fitting, El Dorado, the City of Gold was famous, but South America was always famous about its emeralds if not more famous, to this day - while gold is more like a North America thing, gold fever and such)<br /> Now the problem is? I can't find it...<br /> Maybe it was just a dream<br /> But I had a similar problem with Niflheim, the &quot;Dark Kingdom of Ice&quot; (where from the Queen of the Dead rules from her seat in her capitol city of Hel. The city of Hel lies amidst an icy mountain chain, and overlooks a deep abyss that supposedly drops straight into the Abyss. Within the naturally occurring ice it is said that many wonders may be found, but also many terrors. So, too, do they claim that a bridge exists in the mountains that leads to the land of the fey) untill with the help of the forum managed to track down that elusive afterlife and we discovered, it was mentioned in Dark Ages Mage...<br /> Maybe the Dark Kingdom of Emerald was also mentioned in some other game line's supplement?<br /> Long story short, I don't know<br /> <br /> Any help regarding this nagging question behind my back would be appriciated^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:59:11-07:00","id":1516617,"title":"","content":"This one you're not dreaming: the Dark Kingdoms of Emerald gets a paragraph on page 101 of the Book of Oblivion - they were the Colombian Kingdoms, not Brazilian. The Lands of Gold was the general term for the Kingdoms of South America, including the Dark Kingdoms of Emerald and Tawantinsuyu, the Inka Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T02:23:05-07:00","id":1516624,"title":"","content":"Thank you<br /> I wasn't that far off tho' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Nice to know I'm not totally senile nor dreamed it <br /> I will dust of the Book of Oblivion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T11:08:34-07:00","id":1516673,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Brazil and South America in general - are you familiar with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Skull_Pig\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> bad dudes?<br /> <br /> Because while recently rereading on them i was strongly reminded that there's a lot of folklore about <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peccary\" target=\"_blank\">queixadas</a>,</i> either as soul-stealing pack beasts or as companions to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curupira\" target=\"_blank\">Caipora</a>, in what could be seen as the brazilian spin on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Hunt\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt</a>. Not to mention some northeastern versions of the <i>Lobisomem</i> legend, where actual name notwithstanding, it's described as transforming into a gigantic wild pig. Could there be <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Grondr\" target=\"_blank\">more</a> to the tales than memetic mutation?<br /> <br /> (The fact we have a <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/01/Grondr_forms.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20151113205216\" target=\"_blank\">depiction</a> of one in contemporary clothing - that looks a lot like a <i>caboclo</i> (someone of native american or mixed extraction) to boot - on itself calls to question the rumours of their extinction, i'd say)<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's just the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anhang%C3%A1\" target=\"_blank\">Anhang\u00e1s</a> playing their tricks around...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-29-2023, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:32:13-07:00","id":1516787,"title":"","content":"Yeah, familiar with them, but thank you<br /> And many others, like the Boi-Bumb\u00e1, the Boitat\u00e1, the Mula-Sem-Cabe\u00e7a, Rom\u00e3ozinho, Iara and Mulher de Branco<br /> They will have a hell of time in Brazil <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:57:26-07:00","id":1516869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516609-dark-kingdom-of-emerald?p=1516673#post1516673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe it's just the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anhang%C3%A1\" target=\"_blank\">Anhang\u00e1s</a> playing their tricks around...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>These are interesting creatures that hunt and consume wraiths.<br /> <br /> On a related note how do people portray the Shadowlands and underworld of the rainforests?<br /> <br /> Do they have acres of dark foliage hiding predatory plasms, a landscape of calcified trunks etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T04:48:27-07:00","id":1516879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516609-dark-kingdom-of-emerald?p=1516869#post1516869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a related note how do people portray the Shadowlands and underworld of the rainforests?<br /> <br /> Do they have acres of dark foliage hiding predatory plasms, a landscape of calcified trunks etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark, twisted, death-based reflection of the living world really<br /> A rainforest is the Earth\u2019s most ancient living ecosystem and the lungs of the planet. The oldest fossil records demonstrate that some rainforests have existed in their present form for 50 to 100 million years.<br /> Rainforests have a quality of richness and timelessness, they remind us of our ancestry and the essential nature of life. Entering a tropical rainforest, you immediately sense its vitality, vigor and abundant variety of life<br /> But on the shadowlands, the place of memories.... you will sense the &quot;opposite&quot;.<br /> Eons and milliniums worth of memories of life passed and went extinct, immense loss... and anger, paired with Tempest low rumbling, constant ligthing and thunder, hars wind and plasmic rain, not unlike a maelstorm just in &quot;small&quot;<br /> The memroies and echoes of extinct species and destroyed rainforests, necropoli, ruined remnants of lost civilizations still echoing, half-consumed by &quot;nature&quot; and oblivion<br /> And as you go &quot;deeper&quot; in the shadowlands, closer to the tempest, comes more ancient part most ancient memories, eldich memories even of the forest not really calcified, but obsidian trunks and emerald leaves, dripping with bloody sap - the echoes off screams and bloody sacrifices to long forgetten gods that may have never even existed<br /> Darkness, very dark green, black, the red of blood, and the predatory plasms of predators and flesh eating flowers with the added presence of the Mokol\u00e9 Mnetics, some Dmenkara and quite a few kaiju-like Innocents and Balams who were too curious...<br /> \u200b<br /> Everyting nightmarish the people assoicates with the rainforest based on old stories, warped by their imagination and twisted by death and oblivion<br /> <br /> The Dark Kingdom of Gold, at least in my chronicle is basically El Dorado, the Golden City, stepped piramyds of obsidian and gold ihabited by <i>very angry</i> ghosts - but compared to the rainforest primal nature is quite &quot;tamed&quot; reflecting the civilization that built it<br /> Not unlike the difference between the Shadowlands of the Deserts and Amenti, the Dark Kingdom of Sand<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T08:08:50-07:00","id":1516892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516609-dark-kingdom-of-emerald?p=1516869#post1516869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are interesting creatures that hunt and consume wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anhang\u00e1 portrayal can vary considerably depending on sources - many tales coming from Tupi-guarani communities outside the Amazon frequently emphasized their roles as shapechanging tricksters and/or sorcerers. In my own games, when not in the mood for WtA's baggage, i'd occasionally use a homebrew version of them, more like ghoul families with a common resonance with Protean and strange blood magic rituals involving torpid kindred engulfed in tree-sarcophagy grown from specially prepared stakes, in place of the Changing Breeds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T07:32:29-07:00","id":1516970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516609-dark-kingdom-of-emerald?p=1516879#post1516879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eons and milliniums worth of memories of life passed and went extinct, immense loss... and anger, paired with Tempest low rumbling, constant ligthing and thunder, hars wind and plasmic rain, not unlike a maelstorm just in &quot;small&quot;<br /> The memroies and echoes of extinct species and destroyed rainforests, necropoli, ruined remnants of lost civilizations still echoing, half-consumed by &quot;nature&quot; and oblivion<br /> And as you go &quot;deeper&quot; in the shadowlands, closer to the tempest, comes more ancient part most ancient memories, eldich memories even of the forest not really calcified, <b>but obsidian trunks and emerald leaves, dripping with bloody sap</b> - the echoes off screams and bloody sacrifices to long forgetten gods that may have never even existed<br /> Darkness, very dark green, black, the red of blood, and the predatory plasms of predators and flesh eating flowers with the added presence of the Mokol\u00e9 Mnetics, some Dmenkara and quite a few kaiju-like Innocents and Balams who were too curious...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is great imaginary, definitely stealing - thank you for detailing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T11:12:31-07:00","id":1516984,"title":"","content":"You are welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}